/*
================================================================================
Detection ID:       DET-004
Title:              Suspicious LSASS Process Handle Access (Credential Dumping Indicator)
MITRE ATT&CK:       T1003.001 - OS Credential Dumping: LSASS Memory
Data Source:        Sysmon Event ID 10 (ProcessAccess)
Severity:           High
Author:             Idris Lawan Mustapha
Target Platform:    Splunk Cloud Platform
================================================================================
Description:
Monitors for non-standard process handle requests opened against the Local Security 
Authority Subsystem Service (lsass.exe). Attackers utilize tools such as Mimikatz, 
Meterpreter (hashdump/mimikatz), and ProcDump to access process memory of LSASS to 
extract plaintext passwords, NTLM hashes, and Kerberos tickets.

False Positives:
- Host Antivirus, EDR sensors (CrowdStrike, SentinelOne, Defender), and backup agents
Mitigation / Tuning: Whitelist known endpoint protection executables by binary path, 
hash, and specific granted access rights (e.g. 0x1400 query information).
================================================================================
*/

// Standard Extracted Field Query:
index=main EventCode=10 TargetImage="*lsass.exe*"
| table _time, host, SourceImage, TargetImage, GrantedAccess, CallTrace
| sort -_time

// Correlation Query with Authentication & Privilege Escalation Events:
index=main (EventCode=4624 OR EventCode=4672 OR EventCode=4688 OR EventCode=10)
| table _time, host, EventCode, Account_Name, Image, CommandLine, TargetImage
| sort -_time
